---
title: "publishSaleResults (LegionSealedBidAuctionSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_auth: Legion operator invokes publishSaleResults(claimRoot, acceptedRoot, totalTokens, decimals, privateKey)
    q_check_auth --> q_revert_auth: caller is not Legion operator
    q_revert_auth --> [*]: revert Unauthorized
    q_check_auth --> q_check_locked: caller is Legion operator
    q_check_locked --> q_revert_lock: cancelLocked == false
    q_revert_lock --> [*]: revert NotInitialized
    q_check_locked --> q_check_published: cancelLocked == true
    q_check_published --> q_revert_dup: results already published
    q_revert_dup --> [*]: revert AlreadyPublished
    q_check_published --> q_verify_key: results not yet published
    q_verify_key --> q_revert_key: privateKey does not match publicKey
    q_revert_key --> [*]: revert InvalidPrivateKey
    q_verify_key --> q_set_results: privateKey verified against publicKey
    q_set_results --> q_store_key: set Merkle roots, totalTokensAllocated, decimals
    q_store_key --> [*]: store privateKey; emit SaleResultsPublished(privateKey)

    note right of q_verify_key
        INV-001: Private key must cryptographically match the ECIES public key from initialization
        INV-002: Private key release enables public bid verification
        INV-003: Results can only be published after cancelLocked is true (initializePublishSaleResults called)
    end note
